From: WSLg local integration
Subject: [PATCH] waylandim: forward v1 keyboard modifiers to the client

Backport the modifiers request present in upstream Fcitx 5.1.13 to 5.1.7.
Without it Weston forwards unconsumed raw keys but the application's
wl_keyboard modifier state stays unchanged during the IME keyboard grab.

Upstream reference:
https://github.com/fcitx/fcitx5/blob/5.1.13/src/frontend/waylandim/waylandimserver.cpp

--- a/src/frontend/waylandim/waylandimserver.cpp
+++ b/src/frontend/waylandim/waylandimserver.cpp
@@ -537,6 +537,8 @@
     if (mask & server_->stateMask_.meta_mask) {
         server_->modifiers_ |= KeyState::Meta;
     }
+
+    ic_->modifiers(serial_, mods_depressed, mods_latched, mods_locked, group);
 }
 
 void WaylandIMInputContextV1::repeatInfoCallback(int32_t rate, int32_t delay) {
